                <pb facs="0813" n="797" sameAs="frus:frus1950v01/pg797"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>Concerning the preparation for the Torquay negotiations, a principal function of
                    the Department was to send on to the President the recommendations of the
                    Interdepartmental Committee on Trade Agreements (TAC), the highest-level
                    policy-formulating source in the Executive Branch with respect to United States
                    policy regarding the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT). In this
                    connection, the Department of State submitted to the President during the course
                    of the year some dozen or so “critical” recommendations, ranging in date from
                    March to October. In a sense, these all came into focus in the memoranda of
                    September 26, which are printed below together with certain documentation of
                    subsequent date that arose out of a question left unsettled by the September 26
                    proposals.</p>
            </div>
